## Firmware Testing Strategy

Three layers: (1) host unit (Unity/Ceedling + mocks), (2) on-device integration, (3) HIL smoke. Recipes: `.cursor/skills/sc-firmware/references/verification.md`.

### Must

- Mock all hardware interfaces in host unit tests - never include real vendor HAL/SDK headers in pure logic tests
- Cover error paths and state-machine transitions (timeout, CRC fail, overflow, every event × state when in scope)
- Target/integration: verify peripheral init + basic I/O; ISR latency budget < 10μs when claiming IRQ timing
- Capture verify evidence with `spacecraft evidence` for host and HIL commands used as acceptance
- Static analysis (cppcheck or clang-tidy plus warnings-as-errors) when claiming flight-grade

### Must not

- Claim host-unit green as proof of hardware paths that need target or HIL
- Skip CRC / boundary / timeout cases when the module under test owns that logic
- Treat a single UART boot message as full HIL coverage when a protocol or peripheral suite is in plan scope
